{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 42, :comments ["<b>And he placed it on Joseph's hand.</b> Pharaoh said: perhaps this one's words are not sincere, and he said this only to free himself from me. I will test him with the matter: I will give him the dominion — if he accepts it, his words are certainly sincere, for one would not be so brazen as to enter into greatness from which he will not ultimately endure." "<b>Garments of fine linen.</b> For in Egypt only kings and nobles wear them." "<b>A chain of gold.</b> From the language of מרבדים, רבדתי ערשי; *fermail* in Old French."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {2 "Old French *fermail* (spelled פרמנ״ץ in the manuscript) denotes a clasp or brooch; the root רבד is here associated with overlaying or decking."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:08:18.141170340Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}